How on earth does that calculate anything securely? I mean, if I throw my data in a hat, anyone can pull it out.

10:55.780 --> 11:03.220
Because they don't throw raw data in. They do it by encoding their input as a randomized group element before it ever leaves their hands.

11:04.120 --> 11:08.600
Let's look at the simplest possible example to kind of ground the OR function.

11:08.820 --> 11:09.020
Okay.

11:09.180 --> 11:20.200
Let's say we have three people, Alice, Bob, and Charlie, and we want to know if any of them has a 1, but nobody wants to reveal their specific number. Maybe a 1 means they have a highly stigmatized medical condition.

