So the evaluator looks at the final sum. If it's the baseline 0, they know the answer to the OR function is 0. If it's literally any other random garbage, they know the answer is a 1. Someone has the condition.

12:48.780 --> 12:59.780
But because the randomness thermalized the entire sum, they have absolutely no idea who put in the 1. Did Alice put it in? Did Bob? Did both of them? The provenance is totally annihilated.

12:59.980 --> 13:09.620
Yes. The presence of a single active participant thermalizes the entire sum. One unit of entropy injection masks the entire microscopic configuration.

