But an OR function is incredibly simple, right? It's just a binary yes or no. You mentioned Botansky's 2025 paper proved this framework is universal, meaning you can compute any complex algorithm, not just an OR function. How do you get from a simple yes-no shuffle to computing literally anything?

13:49.280 --> 13:56.540
They do it through a brilliant two-stage process called entropy amplification. First, they build what's called a leaky RE, or layer.

